==Features and Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Spring of Power is an [[Ancient Hylian Ruin]] located in [[Deep Akkala]].<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 413}}</ref> A tunnel from the [[Ordorac Quarry]] serves as the entrance to the Spring. It features a large [[Goddess Statue]] known as the [[Spring of Power Statue]] at its center, which is flanked by two [[Tree]]s. [[Waterfall]]s flow down from a ring on a higher level, which supply the [[Water (Terrain)|Water]] for the Spring. When [[Link]] approaches the Goddess Statue, he will be able to exchange [[Spirit Orb]]s for [[Heart Container]]s or [[Stamina Vessel]]s.<ref>{{Cite|It appears you have claimed {{Color BotW|Red|four}} {{Color BotW|Blue|Spirit Orbs}}. In exchange for {{Color BotW|Red|four}} {{Color BotW|Blue|Spirit Orbs}}, I will amplify your being. So tell me what it is that you desire.|Spring of Power Statue|BotW}}</ref> The [[Dragon]], [[Dinraal]], has served the Spring of Power since ancient times.<ref>{{Cite|A spirit of fire has taken the form of this giant dragon. Making its home in the Eldin region, it's said to have served the Spring of Power since ancient times. An old saying goes, "The dragon ascends to the heavens as the sun begins to set," but nobody has witnessed this in the current age. The flames that coat its body make it dangerous to get near, but Dinraal bears no ill will toward people.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 158}}</ref>

Prior to the second [[Great Calamity]], [[Zelda]] would frequent the Spring of Power in an attempt to awaken her sealing powers.<ref>{{Cite|I've prayed at the Spring of Courage and at the Spring of Power, yet neither awoke anything inside me.|Princess Zelda|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 379}}</ref> In the "[[Slumbering Power]]" [[Recovered Memory]], Link accompanies Zelda as she visits the Spring of Power in an attempt to awaken her sealing power.<ref>{{Cite|Zelda engages in a sacred ritual at the Spring of Power in hopes of awakening her sealing power, but she is overcome with the frustration and seeming futility of her dedication.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|I come seeking help... regarding this power that has been handed down over time... Prayer will awaken my power to seal Ganon away... Or so I've been told all my life...|Princess Zelda|BotW}}</ref> In the middle of her prayer, she becomes frustrated that her power has remained dormant.<ref>{{Cite|And yet... Grandmother heard them—the voices from the spirit realm. And Mother said her own power would develop within me. But I don't hear...or feel anything!|Princess Zelda|BotW}}</ref> She recounts that her father, [[King Rhoam]], has been scolding her for researching [[Ancient Technology]].<ref>{{Cite|Father has told me time and time again... He always says, "Quit wasting your time playing at being a scholar!"|Princess Zelda|BotW}}</ref> Zelda curses [[Hylia]], and she begins to cry as she wonders what is wrong with her.<ref>{{Cite|Curse you... I've spent every day of my life dedicated to praying! I've pleaded to the spirits tied to the ancient gods... And still the holy powers have proven deaf to my devotion. Please just tell me... What is it? What's wrong with me?!|Princess Zelda|BotW}}</ref> After receiving the "[[Captured Memories]]" [[Main Quest]], Link can recall this Memory at the Spring of Power.

At [[East Akkala Stable]], [[Nobo]] will share a legend about offering a "sacred article" to the Spring of Power, which she believes could be part of the rituals Zelda performed.<ref>{{Cite|Let's see... If you go {{Color BotW|Red|west}} of the stable, there's a sacred place called the {{Color BotW|Red|Spring of Power}}! "Offer the {{Color BotW|Red|sacred article}} to the Spring of Power." That's what the legend days. Maybe it was part of a ritual the {{Color BotW|Red|princess}} of {{Color BotW|Blue|Hyrule Castle}} used to perform?|Nobo|BotW}}</ref> Listening to this begins "[[The Spring of Power]]" [[Shrine Quest]]. The first time Link enters the Spring of Power, Hylia will speak through the Goddess Statue, instructing him to offer [[Dinraal's Scale]] to the Spring.<ref>{{Cite|... You have done well to find this spring. Offer {{Color BotW|Red|Dinraal's scale}}, received from the red spirit, to the {{Color BotW|Blue|Spring of Power}}. I, Goddess Hylia, will guide you.|Goddess Statue|BotW}}</ref> If Link does so, the door behind the Statue will open, allowing him to access [[Tutsuwa Nima Shrine]].<ref>{{Cite|Your path has shown itself. Now go forth.|Goddess Statue|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|When you carried out the statue's suggestion and dropped Dinraal's scale into the Spring of Power, an ancient shrine revealed itself.<br/><br/>So the sacred relic was indeed Dinraal's scale...|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

[[File:BotW Korok Seed Icon.png|left|40px]]
A single [[Korok Seed Puzzle]] can be found in the Spring of Power. On the ledge above the main level, there is a [[Rock]] that serves as a [[Natural Hiding Spot]]. When Link picks it up, a [[Korok]] will appear and give him a [[Korok Seed]] as a reward.<ref>{{Cite|Yahaha! You found me!|Korok|BotW}}</ref>

